          <change when="2012-07-03T02:59:38.454-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/Zoom">Vote - Accept-Straight-to-Finalization - taking into account Josh's hesitations, σφηνῶν --&gt; σ̣φ̣ηνῶν</change>
          <change when="2012-07-03T02:59:38.426-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/joshuad.sosin">Vote - DEFER - In lin4 σφηνῶν strikes me as a plausible suggestion, and I think I can see it on the plate. But I am not without doubts. The descender of the φ is much more angular than in Φαμενω&lt;θ&gt; (15). Also, unless I misread or misunderstand, the descender is far off-center to the right of the φ's circular center. The putative φ, then, looks a lot like -εu- in ζεῦγο̣ς in lin13. A nominative is desired and so -γοὶ has the advantage of sense. But "masons of wedges" seems an awkward construction to me. So, this seems plausible, and the agreement of the editor, HC, carries significant weight. But best in my view to hear other editors' voices before proceeding.</change>
